  "body": "The generated resident Heart launcher previously imported the constructor's globally installed `mantleos` package. After assimilation, this could execute a different runtime from the organs shipped inside the NEST.\n\nLaunch Python in isolated mode and explicitly load `mantle/runtime/mantleos`. Refuse installation or startup when the local package is missing or its directory is redirected. Include the runtime and interpreter in the registration receipt and refresh the public Hermes seed.\n\nValidation: 73 local tests, Ruff, public-tree audit, and seed checksum verification pass. A real disposable subprocess with authenticated encryption exercises startup, committed communication without MIND, forced stop/restart, recovery of a pending host receipt, unchanged sealed Primer, and native Body output. Additional tests cover unrelated working directories, Python import-path interference, missing organs, and Windows/Linux registration command construction.\n\nAdvances #16. Task Scheduler/systemd installation and automatic restart are still unverified; registration tests remain mocked. No OS resident registration is performed by this test suite.\n",
